ent um real changes at the gsb  around diversity programming um  was i think it was the most like  um gratifying like part because i felt  like it was something i was giving  rather  than taking again going back to that  that theme  um and now i oh and and touchy feely  and you'll hear this a lot from a lot of  gsb students  um it's a class called interpersonal  dynamics and i feel like  it really i feel like so equipped to  deal with the world  now um and to deal with really difficult  situations  and experiences in a way that um  i didn't necessarily before and i feel  like i have a very  strong sense of who i am for the good  and for the bad  that nothing surprises me anymore um we  just did 360 reviews at work and i was  like yep i've heard all this before both  the good and the best like  nothing was i'm so used to giving and  receiving feedback  um and feel super comfortable with it i  guess i talked about all of them but  it's hard to  to dip in point one um  and yeah i i tell everyone i'm like  everyone do a talk like it really  is when in your life are you gonna have  time to just sit down and reflect on who  you are and what's made you you and then  have a whole group of people just listen  to you and only be focused on you  it was like the only time the dsp phones  were away like  people were laser focused on the person  speaking  um it was like it was like a sacred i'm  not a religious person but it was a  sacred time at the gsb  that was just so so special um and to be  a part of it  um and now i have this this video i get  to keep forever and like showing my kids  um it's just so so special  i know we have limited time just guess  i'll be short um  actually my experiences so they're  they're related to each other the timing  thing so ask someone who was going back  to the exact same thing i was doing  it's very easy to say that two years is  either investment  or potentially even you know i'm making  less than my peers  who stayed at the firm did um but i  think i am going back  a different a different kind of leader  and i was an arbuckle fellow so tied to  sam's experience of touchy-feely being  able to take that early  um in my mba one experience and just  really  understand like how i am landing on  other people um  and it actually inspired me to really go  back to bain because  i know that when i go back i can lead a  team pretty early on  and i will lead it in a completely  different way than i than i would have  two years ago and i have  the our book a leadership program to  thank for that um and the last thing  i'll make a plug for  is and me and a couple of classmates  organized this workshop  called dream big league bully for um  black college students  looking looking to develop their careers  not even into business school  and doing that one with some of my best  friends who i think we will forever  remember how we felt that day when we  put on a virtual event in the  height of covid but also acknowledging  that it was because we came to stanford  and had this network and had  all of these resources just thrown at us  that we were able to have the kind of  impact that we did  i think it served as like a really  really powerful reminder for me that  my education isn't just for me and it  isn't just  to develop my leadership and my career  and my skills all of which are true but  that this experience has given me a  platform and has given me a privilege to  really give back  um to people who may not have the same  sorts of access or opportunities so  i just wanted to put a quick plug even  though that's not technically a stanford  experience it definitely has defined a  lot of the way that i've seen the gsb  and just know that so many of our  classmates are going to go go back to  their communities and give back  in the same way  i love that thank you so much so that is  our program  for today thank you to our attendees for  spending a bit of your day with us and a  huge thank you  to our panelists thank you so much for  sharing your stories sharing your  experiences and your perspectives  i feel really grateful to have had this  opportunity to hear about  what your lives at the gsb and beyond  have been like  so i want to again say thank you and to  everybody  online take care and have a great rest  of your day  thanks everyone

